infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Decompose by layer vs by capability
  desc Same microservices cost — only capability decomposition buys autonomy
  compares
    - label Decompose by layer
      children
        - label 3 network hops per request
          desc presentation to logic to data, where zero were needed
        - label Cannot deploy independently
          desc one rule change forces a coordinated deploy of all three
        - label Cannot test independently
          desc the logic service has no behavior without the data service
        - label Distributed coupling, no autonomy
          desc microservices operational cost with none of the benefit
    - label Decompose by capability
      children
        - label Owns its full vertical slice
          desc API, logic and persistence in one service
        - label Deploys independently
          desc ship the capability without touching the others
        - label Tests independently
          desc the vertical slice has behavior on its own
        - label Fails in isolation
          desc autonomy — the actual microservices payoff
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
